  "_tile_maps": "PHANT.OBJ's wilderness view (live s220): 10 x 9 cells of 2 x 2 PSET0 characters (16 x 16), the party on view cell (4, 4); tile b = DATA's four character / colour-RAM tables at b, multicolour on black with $D022 1, $D023 5. tile_swaps: Scandor's DOS bytes drawn as the C64 tile found in their cells (P3C64ArtManifest.ScandorSwaps) [~]. Near the map's edges the view stops as the remaster's other packs do (the C64's edge rule not read) [~]. Dungeon (DUNGEON.OBJ, live s220): the whole 24 x 30 level in 6 x 3-pixel cells (3 x 3 multicolour sprite pixels; sprite colour 5, $D025 7, $D026 12, black ground), glyphs from the table at runtime $6E77: 0 blank, 1 grey (walls and cells not yet seen), 2 dot, 3 upright bar, 4 level bar, 5 exit, 6 party (drawn instead of its cell). Bytes 200-214 (doors) and 215 seen live; 185-199 and 221+ by DOS's ranges [~]. The upright bar's fourth row, which the C64 draws into the next cell's top row, is left out.",
